comments.body:
stress is factor in heart disease, no?  the current gender stereotype has young men as low-achieving slackers and women as diligent worker-bees disappointed in love & marriage.  perhaps the latter archetype entails more stress.

in my own experience, women internalize stress & emotional upset more than men (whose violence is more outward, e.g., drunken misbehavior.)

if this idea holds water, women might do well to hold feelings less; perhaps go out in woods, push knock over dead trees.)
